	(text_box "This part is not strictly nessesary, it is insurance against unforseen extra bus capacitance from the FFC or mask PCB.\nThis targets I2C FM (400 kHz), which has a bus capacitance limit of 400 pF.\n\nA conservative estimate of worst-case bus capacitances across the downstream system is as follows:\n	Cable (1 m FFC): 40 pF\n	Downstream I2C switch (TCA9546APW): 19 pF (input side) / 6 pF (per channel, 4 channels total)\n		Worst-case devices on one switch channel: 30 pF\n		Worst-case trace capacitance on one switch channel: 50 pF\nWorst-case scenario (All switch channels enabled): 403 pF (already over limit)\n\nAs capacitance estimates are conservative worst-case and there is no reason for all switch channels to be enabled, it is unlikely for the worst-case scenario to occur.\nThis component is included to increase the safety margin should a lesser event occur."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.67 83.8201 0)
		(size 137.16 29.2099)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3421157c-5954-4017-a535-bb6571f8c87e")
	)
	(text_box "Provides a method to determine if the cable is seated correctly in hardware.\nThe pins for presence detection are shorted to ground on the mask PCB."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 39.37 151.13 0)
		(size 80.01 6.3499)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
